":"Jönsson, Li","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah","key":"fdilialaouipedh","last":"Fdili Alaoui","name":"Fdili Alaoui, Sarah","rank":15,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cristopher","key":"aledantecpedh","last":"A. Le Dantec","name":"A. Le Dantec, Cristopher","rank":16,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3656156.3658406","eisbn":["9798400706325"],"pages":"441-444","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","status":"p","subtitle":"Companion Publication of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference","title":"DIS '24 Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198901014"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-146f9ce8-8389-4bf3-9223-3d4dead9340e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Memoirs for the Future, Imaginations of the Past : Crafting Samplers for Intent and Commitment","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752628","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper is a call to study how we attune differently to the care technologies (tech) we live with as a means to design them better. Care tech fiddles with our most intimate relations and vulnerabilities. People have different experiences, dreams, desires, and action potentials, and if they cannot attune to a care tech, the care tech will not work as intended or even cause pathogenic vulnerability. The first part of the paper develops this argument, while the second part analyses three design cases and sketches an approach of deeply situated design as a potential answer to the call.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789561"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Attunement","Care Technologies","Vulnerability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attuning to care technologies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/07370024.2023.2300805","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789561","identifier":[{"id":"85181486285","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7ce8c40a-7005-4407-a71a-1723173920c3"],"keyword":["attunement","care technologies","deeply situated design","design cases","vulnerability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-81844D7616CBB44BF3A9F1493C0E1F74"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/07370024.2023.2300805","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/07370024.2023.2300805","issn":["07370024","15327051"],"issn_org":["07370024"],"journal":"Human-Computer Interaction","pages":"1-12","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181486285"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7ce8c40a-7005-4407-a71a-1723173920c3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Attuning to Care Technologies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789561","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Artifcial Intelligence (AI) repeatedly match or outperform radiologists in lab experiments. However, real-world implementations of radiological AI-based systems are found to provide little to no clinical value. This paper explores how to design AI for clinical usefulness in diferent contexts. We conducted 19 design sessions and design interventions with 13 radiologists from 7 clinical sites in Denmark and Kenya, based on three iterations of a functional AI-based prototype. Ten sociotechnical dependencies were identifed as crucial for the design of AI in radiology. We conceptualised four technical dimensions that must be confgured to the intended clinical context of use: AI functionality, AI medical focus, AI decision threshold, and AI Explainability. We present four design recommendations on how to address dependencies pertaining to the medical knowledge, clinic type, user expertise level, patient context, and user situation that condition the confguration of these technical dimensions.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Zajac, Hubert Dariusz","Ribeiro, Jorge M.N.","Ingala, Silvia","Gentile, Simona","Wanjohi, Ruth","Gitau, Samuel N.","Carlsen, Jonathan Frederik","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Andersen, Tariq Osman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811337"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Kenya"],"glorg":["Aga Khan University","All Global Affiliations","The Nairobi Hospital"],"keyword":["Human Centred AI","Machine learning","Performance optimisation","Transferability","Usability","User centred design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"it depends configuring ai to improve clinical usefulness across contexts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660707","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-811337","identifier":[{"id":"85200350427","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e70f5a4a-5d9b-4e73-bda9-a7eb08d4c7da"],"keyword":["AI Interaction","Human-Centred AI","Machine Learning","Performance Optimisation","Transferability","Usability","User-Centred Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-54CC136E45099F2BBEDD3D3F0F3698C1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660707","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/444201270/It_depends.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centred Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ke","key":"the nairobi hospital","loc":["Kenya","Africa"],"name":"The Nairobi Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ke","key":"aga khan university","loc":["Kenya","Africa"]