{"abstract":"This short paper offers a rationale and manifesto for a design-led research project called careful devices—domestic healthcare technologies that seek to bridge the gap between the lived experience of a person and the abstracted medical knowledge of a health practitioner. The rationale places careful devices at the intersection of contemporary trends in self-tracking and health care technology, and explains how and why this intersection is relevant for future interaction design. This is followed by a manifesto that articulates design goals for producing devices linking these trends, creating a space for interaction design research. We end with a discussion of Ovum, an example of a careful fertility tracking device.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Homewood, Sarah","Almeida, Teresa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381296"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CARE","Futures","Health","Interaction","Research through Design","Speculation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"careful devices a design manifesto for humane domestic healthcare technology","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84703912/HttF_Careful_Devices_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381296","identifier":[{"id":"85076816462","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-02cc008c-840a-417f-9f81-b42ee744c0d7"],"keyword":["care","futures","health","interaction","research through design","speculation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B69895ECD2235DF0BDA927567363863"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https:/