{"abstract":"A recent paradigm shift in healthcare merges the traditional domains of cure and care in healthcare services with prevention and provides all of us with more participation as well as more responsibility in our own healthcare. This shift creates not only a need for personalization of services but also a design challenge with respect to inclusion and acceptance. Healthcare moves into people’s homes and merges medical devices with services hereby enlarging the current contrast between medical device cleanliness and the often cozier and textile-rich home environment. These developments bring important design challenges that will be addressed in this chapter, thereby raising important questions for the implementation of a new design perspective on healthcare.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ludden, Geke D. S.","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381931"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Twente"],"keyword":["Design Challenges","Healthcare Paradigm Shift","Home based Healthcare","Medical Device Integration","Personalized Healthcare"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a design perspective on future healthcare services for the home environment","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85070636794","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381931","identifier":[{"id":"85070636794","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2d2ee618-4cd1-416b-96a5-e267bacc1cfb"],"keyword":["Design Challenges","Healthcare Paradigm Shift","Home-based Healthcare","Medical Device Integration","Personalized Healthcare"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D856C97E27F891A6AE39F970CE9D8680"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"university of twente","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Twente","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Geke D. S.","key":"luddenpau","last":"Ludden","name":"Ludden, Geke D. S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783030007492"],"isbn":["9783030007485"],"pages":"155-167","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Service Design and Service Thinking in Healthcare and Hospital Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070636794"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2d2ee618-4cd1-416b-96a5-e267bacc1cfb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Design Perspective on Future Healthcare Services for the Home Environment","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381931","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Embodied design ideation (EDI) practices work with relationships between body, material and context to enliven design and research potential. Methods are often idiosyncratic and – due to their physical nature – not easily transferred. As independent researchers, and as collaborators, we have been engaging with this problematic for some time. At CHI2017 we will present a framework that enables designers to understand, describe and contextualise EDI practices in ways that can be understood by peers, as well as those new to embodied ideation. Our framework affords discussion of embodied design actions that leverage the power of estrangement. In developing our framework we engaged with numerous researchers who use estrangement as a key activator in embodied design ideation. We thus bring to the workshop (1) a framework to understand and leverage the power of estrangement in embodied design ideation, (2) our individual approaches to EDI, developed over many years of research practice and (3) an inspirational catalogue demonstrating the diversity of ideas that EDI methods can foster.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Wilde, Danielle","Vallgårda, Anna","Tomico, Oscar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-640140"],"event":{"end":"2017-05-06","place":"Denver, us","start":"2017-05-06","title":"Soma-Based Design Theory","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","Elisava"],"keyword":["Design methods","Design research","Disruption","Embodiment","Estrangement","Ideation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"embodied design ideation analysis estrangement and practice","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-640140","ids":["sdu-e9c12624-e997-4536-9d0b-c1ad10e80365"],"keyword":["Design methods","Design research","Disruption","Embodiment","Estrangement","Ideation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-720406ADDBBA52D1BE3ED3DB137CB1CF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design and Communication","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design and Communication, SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"es","key":"elisava","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Elisava","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Danielle","key":"wildepau","last":"Wilde","locid":"5986337f-dcac-47c8-ba45-745fd5223a36","name":"Wilde, Danielle","orcid":"0000-0002-0151-3110","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Oscar","key":"tomicopau","last":"Tomico","name":"Tomico, Oscar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e9c12624-e997-4536-9d0b-c1ad10e80365"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Embodied Design Ideation : analysis, estrangement and practice","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-640140","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we propose Experimental Engineering as a way to articulate open- ended technological experiments as a legitimate design research practice. Experimental Engineering introduces a move away from an outcome or result driven design process towards an interest in existing technologies and how they can assist in creating completely new understandings of people, technology, and their interactions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Grönvall, Erik","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382895"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bricolage","Design Research Practice","Experimental Engineering","explorations","material strategy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experimental engineering articulating and valuing design experimentation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82388387/Experimental_Engineering_CameraReady_reduced_ITUversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382895","identifier":[{"id":"85022204569","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6d007e4b-3736-4231-9504-a850d4582ab0"],"keyword":["Experimental Engineering","bricolage","design research practice","explorations","material strategy."],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BA3C14771AB84DC21D570576F931C15B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82388387/Experimental_Engineering_CameraReady_reduced_ITUversion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3064857.3079145","eisbn":["9781450349918"],"pages":"197-201","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 ACM Conference Companion Publication on Designing Interactive Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85022204569"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6d007e4b-3736-4231-9504-a850d4582ab0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Experimental Engineering: Articulating and Valuing Design Experimentation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382895","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Embodied design ideation practices work with relationships between body, material and context to enliven design and research potential. Methods are often idiosyncratic and – due to their physical nature – not easily transferred. This presents challenges for designers wishing to develop and share techniques or contribute to research. We present a framework that enables designers to understand, describe and contextualise their embodied design ideation practices in ways that can be understood by peers, as well as those new to embodied ideation. Our framework – developed over two conference workshops – provides a frame for discussion of embodied design actions that leverage the power of estrangement. We apply our framework to eight embodied design ideation methods. Our contribution is thus twofold: (1) a framework to understand and leverage the power of estrangement in embodied design ideation, and (2) an inspirational catalogue demonstrating the diversity of ideas that embodied design ideation methods can foster.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Wilde, Danielle","Vallgårda, Anna","Tomico, Oscar"],"cuid":["S02-084.71-038321"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","end":"2017-05-11","place":"Denver, us","start":"2017-05-06","title":"2017 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","Elisava"],"keyword":["Design methods","Design research","Disruption","Embodiment","Estrangement","Ideation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"embodied design ideation methods analysing the power of estrangement","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442747/WildeVallg_rdaTomico_Embodied_Design_Ideation_Methods_analysing_the_power_of_estrangement.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-084.71-038321","identifier":[{"id":"85040079284","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-70db34d7-0f40-4c7a-9009-5c961ef8a41d","sdu-b833b081-899b-4479-b569-9de28d755e94"],"keyword":["Embodiment","design methods","design research","disruption","estrangement","ideation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-82D280BD88464C1D562C2DCE78FBFCFA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442747/WildeVallg_rdaTomico_Embodied_Design_Ideation_Methods_analysing_the_power_of_estrangement.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design and Communication","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Design and Communication, SDU Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"es","key":"elisava","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Elisava","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Danielle","key":"wildepau","last":"Wilde","locid":"5986337f-dcac-47c8-ba45-745fd5223a36","name":"Wilde, Danielle","orcid":"0000-0002-0151-3110","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Oscar","key":"tomicopau","last":"Tomico","name":"Tomico, Oscar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3025453.3025873","eisbn":["9781450346559"],"isbn":["9781450346559"],"pages":"5158-5170","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Explore, Innovate, Inspire","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040079284"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-70db34d7-0f40-4c7a-9009-5c961ef8a41d","sdu-b833b081-899b-4479-b569-9de28d755e94"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Embodied Design Ideation Methods: Analysing the Power of Estrangement","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.71-038321","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The goal for this workshop is to further experiment with a venue at CHI for practitioners of research through design to share their work with each other. This workshop, following a successful workshop in CHI 2016, will be centered upon a discussion of objects produced through a research through design process. Bringing together researchers as well as their physical work serves to gain insight into the practices and outcomes of research through design. If research through design is to continue to develop as a research practice for generating knowledge within HCI, this requires developing ways of attending to its made-material outcomes. The premise of this workshop is simple: We need additional social spaces and platforms for interacting with and reflecting upon material design outcomes at CHI. The goal of this workshop is to keep experimenting with such a space, with an emphasis on how prototyping and making in a research through design context produces design things.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Andersen, Kristina","Gaver, Bill","Odom, William","Pierce, James","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383051"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University","Georgia Institute of Technology","Goldsmiths, University of London","STEIM","Simon Fraser University"],"keyword":["HCI research practices","Material design outcomes","Practitioners workshop","Prototyping and making","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the things of design research diversity in objects and outcomes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82437562/ea652_jenkins.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383051","identifier":[{"id":"85019599156","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-78c8d1f3-8918-48dd-bef2-f250ce1fc89f"],"keyword":["HCI research practices","Material design outcomes","Practitioners workshop","Prototyping and making","Research through design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-48563F9E0F26EE8B468AC0DF869F8DB8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82437562/ea652_jenkins.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"steim","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"STEIM","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"goldsmiths university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Goldsmiths, University of London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"simon fraser university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Simon Fraser University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"carnegie mellon university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Carnegie Mellon University","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","name":"Jenkins, Tom","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kristina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Bill","key":"gaverpau","last":"Gaver","name":"Gaver, Bill","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"William","key":"odompau","last":"Odom","name":"Odom, William","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"piercepau","last":"Pierce","name":"Pierce, James","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3027063.3027068","isbn":["9781450346566"],"pages":"652-659","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2017 CHI Conference Extended Abstracts on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019599156"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-78c8d1f3-8918-48dd-bef2-f250ce1fc89f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Things of Design Research: Diversity in Objects and Outcomes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383051","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Soft robots are typically developed with specific functions in mind. What we propose here is to shift focus to their aesthetic and performative qualities as means to open up a larger space of potential expressions and tacit abilities of these animated artefacts. Basically, to focus on the aesthetic potential of the objects through form, material, and movement exploration. As a strategy, we use provocations to broaden the design space with new interactive experiences in the physical realm. We argue that by using provoking performative objects as inspiration we can ultimately design a more connected and bodily engagement with computational devices.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bewley, Harvey","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384344"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design research","Material interaction","Provocation","Soft Robotics","Temporal form","performing objects"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"provoking performing objects expanding the design space for soft robotics","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442613/p243_bewley.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384344","identifier":[{"id":"85022198892","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d1bc5639-629e-48e7-9231-8fcce70681ef"],"keyword":["design research","material interaction","performing objects","provocation","soft robotics","temporal form"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-40B5B1FFFD6925EAB185C6D9ECC5A378"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442613/p243_bewley.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Harvey","key":"bewleypau","last":"Bewley","locid":"5d268f64-6963-4991-9ac4-e7510c0ae705","name":"Bewley, Harvey","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3064857.3079154","isbn":["9781450349918"],"pages":"243-247","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2017 ACM Conference Companion Publication on Designing Interactive Systems","title":"DIS '17 Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85022198892"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d1bc5639-629e-48e7-9231-8fcce70681ef"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Provoking Performing Objects: Expanding the Design Space for Soft Robotics","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384344","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In the near future every other smart material will have computational power embedded in the form of graphene transistors or nanotubes. These will be the ultimate computational composites: materials that hold classic material qualities, such as structural durability, flexibility, texture, weight, and color, but additionally being capable of sensing, actuating, and computing. Indeed, computers will not be things in and by themselves, but embedded into the materials that make up our surroundings. This also means that the way we interact with computers and the way we program them, will change. Consequently we ask what the practice of programming and giving form to such materials would be like? How would we be able to familiarize ourselves with the dynamics of these materials and their different combinations of cause and effect? Which tools would we need and what would they look like? Will we program these computational composites through external computers and then transfer the code them, or will the programming happen closer to the materials? In this feature we outline a new research program that floats between imagined futures and the development of a material programming practice.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Svanæs, Dag"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384784"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Stockholm University"],"keyword":["Computational Composites","Graphene Transistors","Material Programming Practice","Nanotubes","Smart materials"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"material programming","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82382888/MATERIAL_PROGRAMMING.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384784","identifier":[{"id":"85018939771","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-eeb6cd45-99ad-4dad-b873-f5e373bcc7c7"],"keyword":["Computational Composites","Graphene Transistors","Material Programming Practice","Nanotubes","Smart Materials"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6126F664DE2ECDDE18FE69FB0914F9D2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82382888/MATERIAL_PROGRAMMING.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"stockholm university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stockholm University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dag","key":"svanæspau","last":"Svanæs","name":"Svanæs, Dag","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3057277","issn":["10725520","15583449"],"issn_org":["10725520"],"issue":"3","journal":"interactions","pages":"36-41","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"interactions","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018939771"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-eeb6cd45-99ad-4dad-b873-f5e373bcc7c7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Material Programming","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384784","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this pictorial we present the form-giving process of a Hedonic Haptic player, a wearable device that plays vibrotactile patterns on the body. We depict how we explored the aesthetics of the vibrotactile design space, how we constructed a platform as body of a hedonic experience, and how we developed different vibrotactile compositions. These activities collectively show how combinations of experiencing form, composing form, and materializing form can contribute to the aesthetic form-giving practice in interaction design.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Vallgårda, Anna","Cahill, Ben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384814"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics","Haptic interfaces","Pleasure","Vibrotactile"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"giving form to a hedonic haptics player","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82010769/PictorialDIS2017_Final_V2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384814","identifier":[{"id":"85022215742","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f12e922f-0156-415a-a03e-e603b2555656"],"keyword":["Aesthetics","Haptic Interfaces","Pleasure","Vibrotactile"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16FC5BC1ACDA106C10DEDD022387EACC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82010769/PictorialDIS2017_Final_V2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"cahillpau","last":"Cahill","locid":"4b32d446-5acb-42c7-83b2-41ca287d8613","name":"Cahill, Ben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3064663.3064792","isbn":["9781450349222"],"pages":"903-914","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2017 Conference on Designing Interactive Systems","title":"DIS '17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85022215742"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f12e922f-0156-415a-a03e-e603b2555656"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Giving Form to a Hedonic Haptics Player","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384814","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this design case we present the Hedonic Haptic Player—a wearable device that plays different patterns of vibrations on the body as a form of music for the skin. With this we begin to explore the enjoyability of vibrations in a wearable set-up. Instead of implementing vibrations as a haptic output for some form of communication we want to explore their hedonistic value. The process leading up to the Hedonic Haptic player served as a first step in getting a grasp of the design space of vibrotactile stimuli in a broader sense. This is reported as seven episodes of explorations. The Hedonic Haptic player is currently equipped with three compositions, including an ambient, a rhythmic, and a combination of the two. We explore the value of the experiences they afford through two types of design critique, one from external experts and one auto-critique. We conclude that the vibrotactile stimuli we have created seems to be an acquired taste but that they can indeed create some novel and enjoyable experiences.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Cahill, Ben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382131"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Pleasure","Vibrotactile","haptic design","hedonic design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the hedonic haptic player","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442931/2860_10256_4_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382131","identifier":[{"id":"85040075474","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3af7d376-6ff6-4174-84bc-38034822a3d9"],"keyword":["Pleasure","Vibrotactile","haptic design","hedonic design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-AE5317EBB5C7AD0AEB982BC71B1926D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82442931/2860_10256_4_PB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ijdesign.org/index.php/IJDesign/article/view/2860/789","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"cahillpau","last":"Cahill","locid":"4b32d446-5acb-42c7-83b2-41ca287d8613","name":"Cahill, Ben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19913761","1994036X"],"issn_org":["19913761"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Design","pages":"17-33","publisher":"National Taiwan University of Science and Technology","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Design","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85040075474"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3af7d376-6ff6-4174-84bc-38034822a3d9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Hedonic Haptic Player","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382131","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The Hedonic Haptics player is a portable wearable device that plays back vibrotactile compositions. It consists of three domes each of which houses a vibration motor providing vibrotactile sensations to the wearer. The domes are connected to a control unit the size of a small Walkman. The Hedonic Haptics player can store up to ten different compositions made up of haptic signals varying in amplitude, waveform and length. We use these different compositions to explore the aesthetic potential of vibrational haptics in an embodied wearable setup.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Boer, Laurens","Vallgårda, Anna","Cahill, Ben"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383482"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics","Haptic interfaces","Vibrotactile stimuli","Wearable technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the hedonic haptics player a wearable device to experience vibrotactile compositions","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82010785/Demo_DIS_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383482","identifier":[{"id":"85022220970","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-96c80086-9971-487f-a1ce-9420cb544068"],"keyword":["Aesthetics","Haptic Interfaces","Vibrotactile stimuli","Wearable Technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0762AF97378241F6D28023F76E208E75"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82010785/Demo_DIS_Final.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"cahillpau","last":"Cahill","locid":"4b32d446-5acb-42c7-83b2-41ca287d8613","name":"Cahill, Ben","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3064857.3079178","isbn":["9781450349918"],"pages":"297-300","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2017 ACM Conference Companion Publication on Designing Interactive Systems","title":"DIS '17 Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85022220970"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-96c80086-9971-487f-a1ce-9420cb544068"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Hedonic Haptics Player: A Wearable Device to Experience Vibrotactile Compositions","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383482","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We propose the notion of material programming as a new practice for designing future interactive artifacts. Material programming would be a way for the interaction designer to better explore the dynamics of the materials at hand and through that familiarity be able to compose more sophisticated and complex temporal forms in their designs. As such it would blur the boundaries between programming and crafting these new smart and computational materials. We envision a material programming practice developed around physical tools (e.g. Fig 1) that draw on bodily skills and experiences (Fig 2) while enabling actions performed directly on the material with immediate effects (no program vs. execution mode). Finally, the tools would enable one layer of abstraction and as such encompass the potential of the computational materials but not that of possibly adjacent computers, which could run more complex algorithms.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna","Boer, Laurens","Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Svanæs, Dag"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381637"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","KTH Royal Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Interactive Artifacts","Material Programming","Physical Tools","Smart materials","Temporal Forms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"material programming a new interaction design practice","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84978650812","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381637","identifier":[{"id":"84978650812","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-18c8171c-0bc6-4b54-833d-3bd2c500c498"],"keyword":["Interactive Artifacts","Material Programming","Physical Tools","Smart Materials","Temporal Forms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DE23E7CF55E7C28ED96546A2DC5E128C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"kth royal institute of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KTH Royal Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dag","key":"svanæspau","last":"Svanæs","name":"Svanæs, Dag","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2908805.2909411","eisbn":["9781450343152"],"pages":"149-152","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"DIS '16 Companion","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 ACM Conference Companion Publication on Designing Interactive Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978650812"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-18c8171c-0bc6-4b54-833d-3bd2c500c498"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Material Programming: A New Interaction Design Practice","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381637","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The goal for this workshop is to provide a venue at CHI for research through design practitioners to materially share their work with each other. Conversation will largely be centered upon a discussion of objects produced through a research through design process. Bringing together researchers as well as their physical work is a means of gaining insight into the practices and outcomes of research through design. If research through design is to continue to develop as a research practice for generating knowledge within HCI, this requires developing ways of attending to its made, material outcomes. The premise of this workshop is simple: We need additional spaces for interacting with and reflecting upon material design outcomes at CHI. The goal of this workshop is to experiment with such a space, and to initially do so without a strong theoretical or conceptual framing.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Andersen, Kristina","Gaver, William","Odom, William","Pierce, James","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384007"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University","Georgia Institute of Technology","Goldsmiths, University of London","STEIM","Simon Fraser University"],"keyword":["Design practices","HCI","Interdisciplinary workshop","Material outcomes","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attending to objects as outcomes of design research","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-