{"abstract":"This paper offers a typology for understanding design fiction as a new approach in design research. The typology allows design researchers to explain design fictions according to 5 criteria: (1) “What if scenarios” as the basic construal principle of design fiction; (2) the manifestation of critique; (3) design aims; (4) materializations and forms; and (5) the aesthetic of design fictions. The typology is premised on the idea that fiction may integrate with reality in many different ways in design experiments.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Knutz, Eva","Markussen, Thomas","Christensen, Poul Rind"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-638190"],"event":{"end":"2013-06-12","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2013-06-09","title":"Nordes","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-U"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-ALL","DI-ART-DSKD"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-DSKD","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of fiction in experiments within design art amp architecture","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://nordes.org/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-638190","ids":["sdu-e2dbee0b-60d1-408a-93c2-cb83d5708b61"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-653C7360209051E6FD424A3DF2463665"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.nordes.org/nordes2013/pictures/Nordes2013Proceedings.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://nordes.org/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"design school kolding","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-DSKD","l3nn":"Design School Kolding","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU"