{"abstract":"This panel addresses some of the core aspects of the theme \"It's the experience\", for the CHI2012 conference by focusing on the materials that constitute the foundation for interaction with computers. We take a series of questions as a joint point of departure to consider the nature and character of \"material interactions\" in HCI. Specifically, we consider theoretical, critical and practical approaches to material interactions and how they inform/become useful to HCI. The panel will include position statements from the panelists as well as high-level audience participation. We envision a fun and intellectually stimulating panel moderated by Prof. Mikael Wiberg consisting of a number of scholars with a well-developed view on digital materialities to fuel a discussion on material interactions - from atoms & bits to entangled practices. These scholars include: Prof. Hiroshi Ishii, Prof. Paul Dourish, Daniela Rosner, Petra Sundström, Anna Vallgårda and Tobie Kerridge. This panel also features Mark Rolston, Chief Creative Officer at Frog design, Inc.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383834"],"event":{"end":"2012-05-10","place":"Austin, Texas, us","start":"2012-05-05","title":"The ACM SIGCHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems 2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Critical Perspectives on Interaction","Digital Materialities","Human Computer Interaction HCI","Material interactions","Theoretical Approaches in HCI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"material interactions from atoms amp bits to entangled practices","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2212776.2212408","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383834","identifier":[{"id":"84862662897","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b03a84e8-f99b-4377-b68c-d92d523edb90"],"keyword":["Critical Perspectives on Interaction","Digital Materialities","Human-Computer Interaction (HCI)","Material Interactions","Theoretical Approaches in HCI"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8991A64B5E73BC0AE885F29FAEEE72A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2212776.2212408","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b03a84e8-f99b-4377-b68c-d92d523edb90"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"\"Material interactions\": from atoms &amp; bits to entangled practices","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383834","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
